 35CL    12C(28SI,APG)                 2007KS01,2013BI10,2020RA14ENSDF    202509
 35CL  H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$                                    
 35CL2 H CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2025$                                             
 35CL  H TYP=FUL$AUT=JUN CHEN, JOHN CAMERON AND BALRAJ SINGH$                   
 35CL2 H CIT=NDS 112,2715 (2011)$CUT=20-Oct-2011$                               
 35CL dL E$Least-squares fitting is done by GLSC (version 19-Aug-2025)          
 35CL c  2007Ks01: two different experiments: one with E=70 MeV {+28}Si beam at 
 35CL2c  BARC-TIFR facility and the second with E=88 MeV {+28}Si beam at NSC    
 35CL3c  facility, both using a target of about 50 |mg/cm{+2} {+12}C on a about 
 35CL4c  10.5 mg/cm{+2} gold backing. |g rays were detected with almost         
 35CL5c  identical (INGA) arrays eight Compton-suppressed Clover HPGe detectors.
 35CL6c  Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin, |g|g(|q)(DCO), |g|g(lin pol),            
 35CL7c  Doppler-shift attenuations. Deduced levels, J, |p, T{-1/2}, |g-ray     
 35CL8c  multipolarties and mixing ratios . Comparisons with available data and 
 35CL9c  large-scale shell-model calculations                                   
 35CL c  2013Bi10: E=110 MeV {+28}Si beam was produced from the IUAC-New Delhi  
 35CL2c  accelerator facility. Target was 50 |mg/cm{+2} thick {+12}C on 18      
 35CL3c  mg/cm{+2} Au backing. |g rays were detected with the INGA array of     
 35CL4c  thirteen Compton-suppressed Clover detectors. Measured E|g, I|g,       
 35CL5c  |g|g-coin, |g|g(|q)(DCO), Doppler-shift attenuations. Deduced levels,  
 35CL6c  J, |p, T{-1/2}, evidence for an SD band, |g-ray multiporities.         
 35CL7c  Comparison with large-scale shell-model calculations, two-level mixing 
 35CL8c  calculation, and with structure of SD states in {+36}Ar                
 35CL c  2020Ra14: E=110 MeV {+28}Si beam was produced from the 15UD Pelletron  
 35CL2c  accelerator at the Inter-University Accelerator Centre (IUAC), New     
 35CL3c  Delhi. Target was 50 |mg/cm{+2} {+12}C evaporated onto 18 mg/cm{+2} Au 
 35CL4c  backing. |g rays were detected with a multi-detector array (Indian     
 35CL5c  National Gamma Array) consisting of 13 Compton-suppressed clovers.     
 35CL6c  Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin, |g|g(DCO), |g|g(ADO), |g|g(IPDCO).       
 35CL7c  Deduced levels, J, |p, |g-ray multipolarities. Comparisons with        
 35CL8c  theoretical calculations.                                              
 35CL c  Other reaction:                                                        
 35CL c  1982Le04: {+28}Si({+12}C,X|g) {+12}C (E{-cm}=23-35 MeV) beam produced  
 35CL2c  from the University of Washington FN Tandem Van de Graaff. A target of 
 35CL3c  100 |mg/cm{+2} {+28}Si on a thick tantalum backing. A Ge(Li) detector. 
 35CL4c  Measured |s(E), E|g.                                                   
 35CL c  1985Kr21: {+27}Al({+12}C,X) E=85 meV/nucleon. Measured                 
 35CL2c  particle-particle angular correlations.                                
 35CL cG $|D{-IPDCO} corresponds to integrated polarization asymmetry           
 35CL2cG measurement at E=70 MeV at TIFR facility (2007Ks01). The values are    
 35CL3cG from e-mail reply of Dec 1, 2006 from one of the authors (M. Saha      
 35CL4cG Sarkar) of 2007Ks01 to the previous evaluator B. Singh.                
 35CL cG $|D{-IPDCO} and DCO under comments are from 2007Ks01, unless otherwise 
 35CL2cG noted. Positive value of |D{-IPDCO} indicates electric character and   
 35CL3cG negative value indicates magnetic character. Expected value of DCO is  
 35CL4cG |?1.0 for a stretched transition gated by a transition of same         
 35CL5cG multipolarity, |?2.0 for dipole when gated by a stretched quadrupole   
 35CL6cG (DCO(Q)) and |?0.5 for stretched quadrupole when gated by a stretched  
 35CL7cG dipole (DCO(D)) (2007Ks01). Values deviating from above values indicate
 35CL8cG a mixed transition. DCO values are also available in 2020Ra14, but     
 35CL9cG expected values are opposite to those in 2007Ks01 for stretched dipole 
 35CLAcG and quadrupole transitions when gated by a transion of different       
 35CLBcG multipolarity, that is DCO(Q)|?0.5 for stretched dipole and DCO(D)|?2.0
 35CLCcG for stretched quadrupole (2020Ra14).                                   
 35CL cG $For ADO ratios under comments from 2020Ra14, expected values are 0.6  
 35CL2cG for pure dipole transitions and 1.6 for pure quadrupole transitions or 
 35CL3cG |DJ=0 transitions (2020Ra14)                                           
 35CL cG E$From 2013Bi10, unless otherwise noted                                
 35CL cG RI$From 2007Ks01, measured at E({+28}Si)=88 MeV at the NSC. Values are 
 35CL2cG also available from E=70 MeV data of 2007Ks01 at TIFR facility, but    
 35CL3cG less complete and are given under comments where available.            
 35CL cG M,MR$Q and D+Q with |d(Q/D) are from |g|g(|q)(DCO) in 2007Ks01 and     
 35CL2cG magnetic/electric characters are from |g|g(lin pol) in 2007Ks01 where  
 35CL3cG available and/or RUL where level T{-1/2} is measured, unless otherwise 
 35CL4cG noted.                                                                 
 35CL cG E(X)$From 2007Ks01 only                                                
 35CL cL E$From a least-squares fit to |g-ray energies, assuming |DE|g=1 keV in 
 35CL2cL the fitting procedure.                                                 
 35CL cL J$From Adopted Levels, unless otherwise noted. Adopted assignments for 
 35CL2cL levels in super-deformed (SD) band are from 2013Bi10 in this dataset   
 35CL3cL based on band assignment, with parentheses added by the evaluators.    
 35CL4cL Assignments for tentative levels not adopted in Adopted Levels are     
 35CL5cL proposed by 2007Ks01                                                   
 35CL cL T$From DSAM in 2007Ks01, unless otherwise noted                        
 35CL cL E(B)$Existence of 17/2+ and 21/2+ levels provides indirect evidence in 
 35CL2cL favor of SD band interpretation and parity-doublet cluster structure   
 35CL3cL (2013Bi10)                                                             
 35CL cL T(D)$From DSAM in 2013Bi10                                             
 35CL cL BAND(A)$SD band. Proposed configuration=3p-3h, (sd){+16}(pf){+3}.      
 35CL2cL Negative-parity partner of SD band in {+36}Ar (2013Bi10)               
